\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every Grothendieck coherator C, every cellular C-infinity-groupoid X and every n-cell $a:D_n\to X$, is $X\to X\cup _{D_n}D_{n+1}$, attached along the source inclusion of the next globe, a weak equivalence?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every Grothendieck coherator C, every cellular C-infinity-groupoid X and every n-cell $a:D_n\to X$, is $X\to X\cup _{D_n}D_{n+1}$, attached along the source inclusion of the next globe, a weak equivalence?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/The-Grothendieck-homotopy-hypothesis-via-elementary-expansions-September-24-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

